  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Orks" hidden="false" id="adbe-53b5-788c-2bbb" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="9160-2700-3eb2-858b" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="582d-26d1-b74f-8b66" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Get Stuck In" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="bc37-fd21-3539-03d7">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Trigger: an enemy unit ends a move within 12" of, and in line of sight to, an Ork Infantry or Cavalry unit. The reacting unit immediately moves up to D6 plus its Initiative Characteristic in inches, directly toward the triggering unit, and must end closer to it than it started. If this move ends with the reacting unit engaged with the triggering unit, the reacting unit counts as having charged it, gaining any bonuses for charging, and the combat is fought in the next Assault phase†. The reaction may not be used by a unit that is Pinned, Falling Back, embarked, or already locked in combat.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="The Waaagh!" id="80fd-d26b-fa89-ed7d" hidden="false">
          <description>The Waaagh! is not merely an army, nor even a species-wide instinct for war. It is a psychic phenomenon generated by the collective presence of the Orks themselves, growing larger and more violent as more greenskins gather together for battle. Wherever Ork warbands converge in sufficient numbers, the atmosphere itself seems to thicken with aggression and anticipation. Tempers flare, engines roar louder, weapons malfunction less frequently and even the weakest grot somehow finds the courage to charge directly into gunfire beside his larger kin. To Imperial scholars and Navigators, the Waaagh! manifests as a crude but unmistakable psychic pressure spreading outward from major Ork concentrations like a storm front of violence and instinct.

Unlike the carefully controlled psychic arts of human psykers, the Waaagh! is entirely unconscious. Most Orks possess no understanding whatsoever of the power they generate together, nor would they care if they did. To them, battle simply feels right. The larger the mob grows, the more reality itself bends subtly around their expectations. Engines somehow continue running despite catastrophic damage. Ammunition feeds never seem to empty at the correct moment. Ramshackle war machines surge forward through sheer momentum and improbable luck long after logic insists they should have exploded. Entire Mek workshops produce impossible machines through instinct and collective psychic reinforcement rather than true engineering.

As a Waaagh! expands, its effects become increasingly visible and dangerous. Small warbands may generate only minor battlefield phenomena such as heightened aggression or mechanical resilience, but massive Waaagh!s can destabilize entire systems. Warp routes become erratic, astropathic communication collapses and nearby psykers often report overwhelming psychic noise resembling endless screaming, laughter and gunfire echoing through the Immaterium itself. Weirdboyz become particularly dangerous within large Waaagh!s, acting as living conduits for the accumulating psychic pressure until they either unleash catastrophic displays of power or explode violently beneath the strain.

To the Imperium, the true horror of the Waaagh! is not simply its violence, but its momentum. Every victory strengthens it. Every conquered world feeds it. Defeated enemies provide weapons, vehicles, slaves and raw materials for the next stage of expansion while surviving Orks attract more warbands from across nearby systems. What begins as isolated raids or scattered pirate attacks may rapidly evolve into a sector-wide apocalypse once enough greenskins gather beneath a powerful warlord. Entire Imperial campaigns have collapsed because commanders underestimated how quickly a growing Waaagh! can transform from a localized threat into a civilization-consuming war machine.

At the height of a true Waaagh!, the distinction between military campaign, migration and natural disaster effectively disappears. Countless warbands merge together beneath the largest and strongest bosses while Titans, battlefleets and hive worlds vanish beneath endless tides of green bodies and roaring engines. Even the Traitor Legions and the servants of Chaos have learned to fear such events, for the Waaagh! does not negotiate, retreat or truly end while enemies remain standing. It simply grows larger, louder and more violent until either the galaxy breaks beneath it or the Orks finally find something worthy of fighting.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Waaagh! Doctrine" id="472d-760d-0ddb-d4b5" hidden="false">
          <description>The Waaagh! is more than merely the war cry of the Orks. It is a psychic phenomenon generated by the collective aggression, violence and momentum of countless greenskins gathered together for battle. As Ork armies grow larger and the fighting intensifies, this latent psychic pressure spreads throughout nearby mobs, war machines and Weirdboyz alike, amplifying the destructive instincts of the entire horde. Though few Orks understand the true nature of the Waaagh!, every warband instinctively channels its energy toward the forms of warfare it values most.

Different warbands focus this psychic momentum in radically different ways. Some hurl themselves into direct melee slaughter amidst screaming charges and brutal close combat, while others unleash impossible storms of gunfire or roaring mechanized assaults driven by the momentum of the Waaagh! itself. Amongst the strangest warbands, Weirdboyz and Warpheads manipulate the psychic energy directly, transforming the battlefield into a catastrophic storm of green lightning, exploding reality and uncontrolled Warp manifestations. These battlefield philosophies become known amongst the Orks as Waaagh! Doctrines.

A Waaagh! Doctrine represents the dominant expression of the psychic momentum surrounding an Ork army once battle reaches its peak. Whether through overwhelming violence, impossible speed, endless gunfire or catastrophic psychic power, the Waaagh! focuses itself through the collective instincts of the horde until the entire battlefield descends into barely controlled chaos. Once unleashed, the Waaagh! transforms the Ork warbands from dangerous raiders into an unstoppable tide of destruction capable of overwhelming even the greatest armies of the Imperium.

A Detachment that contains at least one model with the Da Biggest is Da Best special rule may select a single Waaagh! Doctrine. A Waaagh! Doctrine is unleashed when the army calls its Waaagh!: it counts as the army's one Waaagh! call for the battle.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
