                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="17fc-0305-8659-e653" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="ce13-9242-3cf1-ad3b" hidden="false">
                  <description>Squighog Boyz may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Beast Snagga units in a Detachment using this Rite of War re-roll to-wound rolls of 1 against Vehicles, Dreadnoughts and Monstrous Creatures.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="2934-6128-57a4-c42d" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must have a Beastboss, Beastboss on Squigosaur or Mozrog Skragbad as its Warlord. A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Flyers, any Gretchin, or any Heavy Support vehicles other than Kill Rigs and Hunta Rigs. This Rite of War may not be used by an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="f0a1-2757-95d8-1017" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Speed Freeks" hidden="false" id="ccb3-b830-f9f4-48b5" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="instanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="ancestor" childId="d4f2-6da5-b6de-06ec" shared="true" />
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="783c-5937-d041-03a3" hidden="false">
                  <description>Warbikers may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War, and gain the Line sub-type. Nobz on Warbikes may be taken as Fast Attack choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Ork vehicles with the Fast sub-type and Mechanised Ork Cavalry (the Speed Freek buggies) in a Detachment using this Rite of War improve their Ramshackled Vehicle (X) or Ramshackled Carapace (X) by 1, so (6+) becomes (5+).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="ef5b-602e-c34e-38e8" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must have a Warboss or Big Mek on Warbike as its Warlord. Every Infantry unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War must start the game embarked on a Trukk or Battlewagon, or have rokk-packs. This Rite of War may not be used by an Allied Detachment.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="16b8-5fad-296f-7099" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Waaagh! Doctrine" hidden="false" id="91ac-e7b4-a32d-ef29">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="deae-ce8a-a3dd-0a5e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="36b4-af5b-c35a-be53" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="a310-4e70-5397-9815" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f84c-1b57-13b6-1c96" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="797f-04dc-77fb-4579" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier type="set" field="7b9a-ab52-5299-44ef" value="0">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="deae-ce8a-a3dd-0a5e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="36b4-af5b-c35a-be53" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="a310-4e70-5397-9815" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f84c-1b57-13b6-1c96" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                    <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="797f-04dc-77fb-4579" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="7b9a-ab52-5299-44ef" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krumpin' Waaagh!" hidden="false" id="f596-3e7f-076c-51df" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Krumpin' Waaagh!" id="4418-a0ce-257d-cce4" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Krumpin' Waaagh! is the purest expression of Ork brutality unleashed across the battlefield. As the roar of the Waaagh! spreads through the mobs, every Ork surges forward in a tide of violence and momentum that few enemies can survive. Infantry mobs charge headlong into enemy lines while Dreadnoughts and armoured brutes smash through fortifications and infantry alike beneath a storm of gunfire, blades and roaring engines. During a Krumpin' Waaagh!, discipline and caution vanish entirely as the Orks become consumed by the simple joy of close-range slaughter.

To Imperial observers, a Krumpin' Waaagh! resembles less a coordinated military assault and more a natural disaster. Entire front lines collapse beneath the weight of charging greenskins while wounded Orks continue fighting through injuries that should have killed them outright. The psychic momentum generated by the Waaagh! itself drives the Orks into an almost unstoppable frenzy of aggression and destruction.

Once per battle, at the start of any turn, all friendly Ork Infantry and Dreadnought units gain:

• Fleet (2)
• Furious Charge (2)
• Fearless
• Feel No Pain (5+)
• Dakka! (5+)

The effect lasts until the end of the turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Speed Waaagh!" hidden="false" id="415f-4751-f2c4-cd05" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Speed Waaagh!" id="8762-ab7c-a76b-462c" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Speed Waaagh! represents the war doctrines of the Speed Freeks, biker mobs and fast-moving raider warbands that sweep across the battlefield with terrifying speed. Engines scream, exhausts belch fire and entire formations surge forward in clouds of smoke and burning fuel as Warbikes, buggies, jump infantry and ramshackle vehicles hurl themselves into battle. During a Speed Waaagh!, the battlefield becomes a blur of motion where even the largest Ork vehicles move with reckless velocity.

To the Orks, speed itself is a weapon. Fast-moving assaults crash into enemy formations before defenses can react while reserve forces surge unexpectedly into battle amidst clouds of smoke and roaring engines. Entire armoured columns may disappear into dust and debris only to reappear moments later smashing directly into vulnerable enemy positions. The Speed Waaagh! transforms the normally chaotic momentum of the Orks into something terrifyingly mobile and unpredictable.

Once per battle, at the start of any turn, all friendly Ork Cavalry, Jump Infantry, Skirmish and Vehicle units gain:

• Fleet (3)
• Sudden Strike (3)
• Hammer of Wrath (+1)
• Shrouded (5+) while Running

In addition, all friendly Ork units gain +2 to Reserve rolls during this turn.

The effect lasts until the end of the turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Dakka Waaagh!" hidden="false" id="d4b8-aeda-81bf-b112" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Dakka Waaagh!" id="d7c5-6f2b-9226-3c4c" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Dakka Waaagh! is the culmination of every Ork belief that no problem exists which cannot be solved through overwhelming quantities of gunfire. During a Dakka Waaagh!, the battlefield vanishes beneath torrents of shells, tracer fire and ricocheting scrap metal as entire mobs unleash impossible volumes of shooting without concern for ammunition conservation, overheating or basic mechanical safety. Big Shootas roar continuously, Deffguns shake themselves apart under sustained fire and even the largest Ork war engines become mobile storms of bullets and explosions.

Though wildly inaccurate by Imperial standards, the sheer density of fire unleashed during a Dakka Waaagh! is often enough to overwhelm even elite enemy formations through suppression and attrition alone. Entire sectors of the battlefield become impassable beneath the storm of incoming fire while enemy infantry are pinned beneath the relentless noise and violence of the advancing greenskins. The Dakka Waaagh! is not precision warfare. It is destruction through excess.

Once per battle, at the start of any turn, all friendly Ork units gain:

• Dakka! (4+)
• Twin-linked on all Auto weapons
• Pinning on all Auto weapons
• Breaching (6+) on all Auto weapons
• Relentless

In addition, Heavy weapons fired by friendly Ork units gain +1 Shot, to a maximum increase of +3 shots per weapon.

The effect lasts until the end of the turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Odd Waaagh!" hidden="false" id="aeb1-56be-aa5a-ff2b" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Odd Waaagh!" id="b735-1b0b-5625-233f" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Odd Waaagh! represents the terrifying moment when the psychic energy of the Waaagh! becomes concentrated around Weirdboyz, Warpheads and other unstable Ork psykers. As the battle intensifies, the raw psychic pressure generated by thousands of Orks begins boiling over into catastrophic Warp manifestations and impossible surges of power. Weirdboyz become living conduits for the Waaagh! itself, channeling destructive psychic energy across the battlefield with little understanding or control over what they unleash.

To nearby Orks, the presence of an empowered Weirdboy fills them with violent excitement and reckless confidence. Entire mobs charge screaming into battle beneath storms of green lightning and exploding reality while the Weirdboyz themselves teeter constantly upon the edge of catastrophic psychic collapse. Even the Orks rarely understand exactly what an Odd Waaagh! will do once unleashed — only that it will be loud, dangerous and very likely hilarious right up until something explodes.

Once per battle, at the start of any turn, all friendly Weirdboyz and Psykers gain:

• +2 Leadership for Psychic checks
• Adamantium Will (4+)
• Feel No Pain (4+)

All friendly Ork units within 12" of a friendly Weirdboy or Weirdboss gain:

• Counter-Attack (2)
• Furious Charge (2)

In addition, all Weirdboy Psychic Weapons gain Rending (5+) during this turn.

The effect lasts until the end of the turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
