          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="5ee3-be03-2381-b69a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Red-hot Speedboss" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="00ce-be6d-193d-98b9">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord, any unit he joins, and any vehicle he is embarked on add 2 to their Movement Characteristic and gain the Outflank special rule.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="9b6d-86da-6930-89b0" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Kaptin of Kaptins" hidden="true" id="eaee-36a2-02de-93e1" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1f9f-17d3-8ccd-9efd" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3ccc-1a18-6596-6dc8" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Kaptin of Kaptins" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="6836-fb95-3a45-57c5">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord commands through sheer swagger, wealth and reputation amongst the pirate fleets. Friendly Freebooterz units within 12" of the Warlord gain Crusader. In addition, the Warlord gains Preferred Enemy (Characters). An army whose Warlord has this Trait may make one additional Reaction during the opposing player's Shooting phase as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="85a5-a83b-c3cc-291d" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Skarboy Boss" hidden="true" id="8489-3d62-8ea2-aed0" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="22c6-363a-67fd-1836" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1b51-246c-77cb-0df3" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Skarboy Boss" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="8597-9052-ed40-1fcc">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord and any unit he joins gain the Furious Charge (1) special rule, or increase an existing Furious Charge (X) by 1.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="cd9d-c5fc-2985-3ee7" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Rust Masta Mek" hidden="true" id="f9fc-0e20-2c45-416b" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="daf7-991e-bb16-91d2" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2d23-00ba-bd3c-3310" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Rust Masta Mek" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="09c1-4026-d6ac-a834">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord is among the greatest mekboyz of the Waaagh!, capable of keeping entire armoured spearheads fighting long after they should have collapsed. Friendly Rustboyz Vehicles and Dreadnoughts within 12" of the Warlord may re-roll failed It Will Not Die rolls. In addition, one friendly Vehicle within 6" may ignore Crew Shaken results. An army whose Warlord has this Trait may make one additional Reaction during the opposing player's Shooting phase as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="234f-1449-32a5-7c2d" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Beast Tamer" hidden="true" id="dd2e-e50e-f2a3-016d" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7cb2-c4cf-dfb7-3b04" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8cab-877d-9d7b-8878" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Beast Tamer" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="8a3e-b483-3619-0b0a">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">Friendly Snakebite Beast Snagga Boyz, Squighog Boyz and squig-mounted models within 12" of the Warlord may re-roll failed charge distances.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="efe8-e83d-a546-4c96" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Ammo Runts" id="9107-ff91-8a87-766c" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Ammo Runts scurry alongside their masters carrying spare ammunition, replacement magazines and unstable experimental rounds looted from countless battlefields. Once per battle, before making a Shooting Attack, a model accompanied by one or more Ammo Runts may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls and failed To Wound rolls for a single Shooting Attack. After the attack has been resolved, remove one Ammo Runt from play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bigga iz Betta" id="150c-ba53-b501-3917" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Models with the Bulky (X) special rule that join a unit add X to the total number of models in the unit for the purposes of determining Mob Rule bonuses. In addition, Cavalry models count as four models each for the purposes of determining Mob Rule bonuses.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Breakin' Heads" id="740a-e433-bb54-c49d" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If a unit with Mob Rule that includes a Nob, Boss Nob or Ork character fails a Morale check or Pinning test, it may choose to pass it instead. If it does, the unit suffers D3 automatic hits at Strength 6, AP –, allocated by the Ork player to models other than characters; armour saves may be taken.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Da Biggest is Da Best" id="ebb2-7a37-35c8-2c7f" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Among the Orks, leadership belongs only to the strongest, loudest and most violently successful warlords. The greatest bosses dominate their mobs through brute strength, terrifying aggression and the simple certainty that anyone challenging their authority will be beaten to death publicly and immediately. Entire Waaagh!s rise and fall around such figures as lesser Orks instinctively gather beneath the biggest and meanest leaders they can find.

A model with the Da Biggest is Da Best special rule grants the following benefits:

• Waaagh! Leader: If a Detachment contains at least one model with this special rule, that Detachment may select a single Waaagh! Doctrine or equivalent army-wide Ork upgrade if permitted by the campaign organizer.
• The Biggest and the Meanest: An army may only include a maximum of one model with this special rule per 1,000 points.
• Mob Boss: A model with this special rule may select an eligible Retinue or Nob bodyguard unit as part of the same Force Organisation slot.

Da Biggest is Da Best is treated as equivalent to Master of the Legion for the purposes of any campaign rules, mission effects or special interactions that reference Master of the Legion.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dakka! (X)" id="0644-bb6e-7891-7f9f" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When making Shooting Attacks with Auto weapons, unmodified To Hit rolls of X+ generate one additional hit. Additional hits generated in this way do not themselves generate additional hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deadly Demise" id="5b9e-eba9-711d-139a" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When a model with this special rule is destroyed, but before it is removed from play, all units within 6" suffer a Strength 8 AP – hit with Rending (6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deck Crew (X)" id="9aaf-3ec9-c252-3334" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>This weapon can only be used if the vehicle is locked in combat or has been charged. In the Initiative 1 step of the Fight sub-phase, the vehicle model makes a fixed number of attacks equal to X using this profile. These attacks hit automatically if the vehicle is stationary, or hit on a 4+ if the vehicle moved in the preceding Movement phase. These attacks do not benefit from charging or any army-wide special rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dread Mob" id="431f-3f6b-fb9d-4f16" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When deployed onto the battlefield, either at the start of the battle or when arriving from Reserves, all models with this special rule in the same unit must be deployed within unit coherency (3"). After deployment, all models immediately operate independently and are no longer treated as a single unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="'Ere We Go!" id="fe04-50c9-c0ad-8fb5" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When rolling charge distance, the unit may re-roll one of the dice. If the charge still fails, the unit moves the full distance rolled toward the target, instead of the usual reduced failed-charge move†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Exhaust Belch" id="b19a-e1bf-37d3-9a3f" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>After this unit completes a Run move, place a flamer template touching the rear of the model. Any unit touched by the template suffers D3 Strength 5 AP – hits with the Pinning special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fetishes of Gork and Mork" id="3a26-8469-b84b-e8be" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Fetishes of Gork and Mork grant a 4+ Invulnerable Save and Adamantium Will (4+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Attendants" id="67a8-98be-35bc-ea7b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Grot Attendants are grots that are attached to other units. They provide a special bonus to the mob while they are still alive. In addition, they are all armed with a grot blasta and grot stabba unless otherwise noted. A model with this rule does not count towards the unit's size, never gains Klan (X), and may not issue, accept or be chosen for a challenge. Hits can only be allocated to it by attacks with Precision Shots or Precision Strikes. When a Wound would be allocated to another model in its unit, the controlling player may allocate that Wound to a model with this rule instead. If it is removed, any bonus it gives is lost.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Orderly" id="0b0d-ea28-e43e-05ad" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Grot Orderlies are terrified little surgical assistants, pain suppressors and battlefield medics that follow their masters carrying crude stimulants, spare body parts and improvised surgical tools. A model accompanied by one or more Grot Orderlies gains Feel No Pain (6+). If the model already possesses Feel No Pain, improve that roll by +1 to a maximum of Feel No Pain (4+). When a model benefiting from a Grot Orderly fails a Feel No Pain roll, the controlling player may instead remove one Grot Orderly from play. The Grot Orderly suffers the wound instead of the targeted model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Piloted" id="82a3-ba19-93d3-bd40" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>This model may use the Leadership characteristic of the nearest friendly Ork Infantry Character within 12" when making Morale checks and Pinning checks. If no qualifying model is within range, this model suffers −1 Weapon Skill.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Riggers (X)" id="b62c-5ed8-63f2-5b53" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>At the end of each of your turns, roll a D6 for each model with this rule that has lost Hull Points. On a roll of X or more, it restores one lost Hull Point, up to its starting value. A model cannot use Grot Riggers in a turn it was embarked, Falling Back or locked in combat†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Kommando Grot" id="812e-4d9c-ed65-af1d" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Kommando Grots are sneaky little saboteurs, ammunition carriers and lookouts that creep ahead of the main mob marking targets, planting charges and slipping through spaces too small for larger Orks. A unit containing a Kommando Grot gains +1 to all Cover Saves while wholly within terrain. In addition, a unit containing a Kommando Grot gains Precision Shots (6+) during the first turn of the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Luck of Mork and Gork" id="0c0a-a791-55b9-50de" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Gretchin units gain a 6+ Invulnerable Save against attacks made with Blast or Template weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mek-Smasha (X)" id="6989-913d-92e6-2a8b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If a model with the Mek-Smasha (X) special rule is in base contact with, or Embarked upon, one or more damaged Vehicles, Dreadnoughts, Automata, or Mechanized units during the Shooting phase, they can attempt to repair one of them. If they do so, the model that attempted the repair cannot shoot any weapons or use any other abilities that would be used instead of making a Shooting Attack. Roll a D6. If the result is equal to or more than the value listed in brackets as part of this rule, the repair is successful. Apply one of the following options to the target unit the model is in base contact with or Embarked upon: Repair a Weapon Destroyed result. Repair an Immobilised result. Restore a lost Hull Point. Restore a lost Wound. If a Weapon Destroyed result is repaired, that weapon may not be used to attack in the same phase as it is repaired, but may be used to attack as normal in any phase after that. The Mek-Smasha cannot use this ability if they are Pinned or Falling Back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Might iz Right!" id="ebd9-925c-cabf-9b62" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Ork units with the Bulky (X) special rule add X to their Initiative Characteristic while engaged in a Challenge, to a maximum Initiative Characteristic of 7.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mob Rule" id="9986-6062-e065-6f8a" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Any Ork Infantry, Jump Infantry or Cavalry unit that is not a Walker, Grot or Vehicle gains the Mob Rule special rule. If a unit with this special rule contains 10 or more models, it gains Stubborn. If a unit with this special rule contains 20 or more models, it gains Fearless and Rage (2). If a unit with this special rule contains 30 or more models, it gains Fearless and Rage (3).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mob Up" id="b395-add5-c4b4-e188" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Two Ork units of the same type that end their Movement phase within 2" of each other may attempt to Mob Up. To Mob Up, the controlling player must immediately take a Leadership test using the highest Leadership characteristic available between the two units. If the test is passed, the two units immediately merge into a single unit for the remainder of the battle. If the test is failed, both units immediately suffer D6 Strength 6 AP – hits that also inflict Pinning. Only units of the same type may Mob Up. Shoota Boyz may Mob Up only with other Shoota Boyz mobs.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mo' Dakka" id="7c95-1e85-d2ea-dd63" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When a model with this special rule generates an additional hit from Dakka!, the additional hit gains all of the same special rules and effects possessed by the original attack, including Rending, Breaching, Armourbane, Pinning and similar weapon effects.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Odd Mob" id="3c0e-c25a-c45b-9f68" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>The Meks, Painboys and Weirdboys of a warband stand outside the mobs, lending their talents wherever the boss sends them. Only on the longest Waaagh!s would an Odd Boy find himself krumpin' alongside the same lads time and time again. An Odd Mob is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed to the battlefield, each Odd Boy in an Odd Mob, together with any grots he has taken, either becomes a separate unit or is assigned to another unit from the same Detachment of the army the Odd Mob was selected as part of. An Odd Boy may only be assigned to a unit composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type and the same Klan (X) special rule as the Odd Boy, and may not join a unit that includes models in Mega Armour.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Oddboy" id="487b-f932-39ab-f602" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Oddboyz may join Ork units normally, but do not count toward unit size when determining bonuses granted by the Mob Rule special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Oil Runts" id="25c9-098f-a1c7-3184" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Oil Runts are filthy little mechanics and lubricant carriers that swarm over weapons, armour plates and damaged machinery attempting crude battlefield repairs while avoiding being stepped on by their larger kin. Once per battle, at the start of the controlling player's turn, a model accompanied by one or more Oil Runts may immediately regain a single lost Wound or Hull Point. After the repair has been resolved, remove one Oil Runt from play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Open-topped" id="792a-d019-9e41-d7f8" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>The vehicle gains the Assault Vehicle special rule, but adds 1 to its rolls on the Vehicle Damage table when it suffers a penetrating hit. The entire vehicle counts as its Access Point.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ramshackled Carapace (X)" id="2a3f-661c-d22f-ef1b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>This unit is a ramshackle mechanical nightmare held together through crude reinforcement, unstable reactors and the barely competent maintenance of terrified grot crews. Though wildly unreliable, these clanking engines of war are often far harder to destroy than logic would suggest. A model with the Ramshackled Carapace (X) special rule gains an X+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, a model with Ramshackled Carapace (X) and a Wounds Characteristic that suffers an unsaved Wound with the Instant Death special rule is not immediately removed as a casualty, but instead loses D3 Wounds for each unsaved Wound inflicted by the attack. When a model with Ramshackled Carapace (X) loses its last Wound, but before it is removed as a casualty, all models, both friendly and enemy, within D6" suffer an automatic Strength 8 AP – hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ramshackled Vehicle (X)" id="d92a-f330-bfcd-9d74" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Ork vehicles are infamous for being impossible creations of crude engineering, scavenged armour plating and dangerously unstable mechanical improvisation. Built from stolen hulls, battlefield wreckage and whatever scrap metal happened to survive the last explosion, these ramshackle machines should barely function at all. Yet through some combination of brutal overengineering, improbable luck and the inexplicable genius of the Ork mekboyz, many continue fighting long after more sophisticated war machines would have been destroyed. A vehicle with the Ramshackled Vehicle (X) special rule gains an X+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, when a vehicle with the Ramshackled Vehicle (X) special rule suffers a Penetrating Hit, roll a D6. On a result of X or greater, the Penetrating Hit is instead treated as a Glancing Hit. However, on a roll of 1, add +2 to the roll made on the Vehicle Damage table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Retinue" id="1d82-3107-8ace-917c" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>A Warboss Retinue may be selected as a Retinue for a Warboss. While joined by the Warboss for whom it was selected as a Retinue: the unit does not use up an additional Force Organisation slot all models in the unit gain the Line Sub-type If the attached Warboss is removed as a casualty, the unit immediately loses the Line Sub-type unless another rule would grant it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runt Orkalytes" id="19f5-7ebe-55fc-9b9a" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>At the beginning of any phase, the controlling player may remove one Runt Orkalyte from play. If they do, the Weirdboy immediately gains +1 Waaagh! Energy until the end of the current turn. If a Runt Orkalyte is removed as a casualty by a Precision Shots or Precision Strikes attack, all units within D6" suffer D3+1 hits at Strength D3+1 and AP D6+1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="4f86-aae1-17da-67cb" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If the model has not moved this turn, it cannot be targeted by ranged attacks from more than 12" away.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Speed Freekz" id="5206-b3f9-c8f4-fee3" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Models with this special rule gain Fleet (2), Sudden Strike (2), and Hammer of Wrath (1). In addition, they may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Hunters" id="cb2f-190f-9b7f-0f1e" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>The model's attacks gain the Sunder special rule. If a weapon already has Sunder, add 1 to its Armour Penetration rolls instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Titanic Presence" id="e9b1-faec-6cf8-b4b0" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Friendly Ork Infantry, Cavalry and Jump Infantry units within 18" of a Stompa gain Stubborn. In addition, friendly Ork units within 18" may use the Stompa's Leadership characteristic of 10 when making Morale checks and Pinning checks. A Stompa also counts as 15 additional models for any special rule or ability that counts the number of nearby Ork models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh!" id="01d0-45ce-18b3-5564" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Once per game, at the start of any turn, if the army's Warlord is an Ork and is on the table, the army may call a Waaagh! If the army includes a model with the Da Biggest is Da Best special rule (a Warboss, Mek Boss, Painboss, Weirdboss or Ghazghkull Thraka), the Waaagh! unleashes the army's Waaagh! Doctrine, one of the following (see Waaagh! Doctrine for the full rules):

• Krumpin' Waaagh!: all friendly Ork Infantry and Dreadnought units gain Fleet (2), Furious Charge (2), Fearless, Feel No Pain (5+) and Dakka! (5+).
• Speed Waaagh!: all friendly Ork Cavalry, Jump Infantry, Skirmish and Vehicle units gain Fleet (3), Sudden Strike (3), Hammer of Wrath (+1) and Shrouded (5+) while Running, and all friendly Ork units gain +2 to Reserve rolls.
• Dakka Waaagh!: all friendly Ork units gain Dakka! (4+) and Relentless, their Auto weapons gain Twin-linked, Pinning and Breaching (6+), and their Heavy weapons gain +1 Shot, to a maximum increase of +3 shots per weapon.
• Odd Waaagh!: all friendly Weirdboyz and Psykers gain +2 Leadership for Psychic checks, Adamantium Will (4+) and Feel No Pain (4+); friendly Ork units within 12" of a friendly Weirdboy or Weirdboss gain Counter-Attack (2) and Furious Charge (2); and Weirdboy Psychic Weapons gain Rending (5+).

The effects last until the end of the turn.

If the army includes no model with the Da Biggest is Da Best special rule, when it calls a Waaagh!, until the end of that turn every unit in it with this rule gains the following:

• Fleet (+1): the unit gains Fleet (1), or increases an existing Fleet (X) by 1.
• Furious Charge (+1): the unit gains Furious Charge (1), or increases an existing Furious Charge (X) by 1.

Units with Mob Rule also automatically pass Morale checks until the start of your next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh! Energy" id="22d5-a04c-eb29-712d" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>A Weirdboy increases its Leadership characteristic by +1 for the purposes of making Psychic checks for every 10 friendly Ork Infantry models within 12", to a maximum bonus of +3. His Leadership can never be raised above 10 by this rule. Models with both the Bigga iz Betta and Bulky (X) special rules count as X additional models for the purposes of determining Waaagh! Energy. The power of the Waaagh! is hard to control: an Ork Psychic check suffers Perils of the Warp on any double, even if the check is passed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Perils of the Waaagh!" id="39f7-c1ce-029c-1605" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>If a Weirdboy fails a Psychic check, it automatically suffers Perils of the Warp. In addition, all units within D6" plus the current Waaagh! Energy bonus suffer D6 Strength 3 AP – hits with the Pinning and Shell Shock (1) special rules. The Weirdboy's current Waaagh! Energy bonus is also added to: the range of the effect the Strength of the hits the number of hits inflicted the value of the Shell Shock special rule Every Weirdboy knows Da Jump and Frazzle. A Weirdboy with the Warphead upgrade also knows Fists of Gork. Power: Kind, Phase, Effect. Da Jump: Psychic power, Movement, Select one friendly Ork unit within 12" of the Weirdboy, plus one more for each +1 of his current Waaagh! Energy bonus. Remove the selected units from the battlefield and place them in Reserves. Roll for them as normal for Reserves, adding the Waaagh! Energy bonus to each roll; when they arrive, they enter play by Deep Strike as normal. The Waaagh! Energy bonus is fixed when Da Jump is cast, and that same value is used for these Reserves rolls.. Fists of Gork: Psychic power, Assault, Until end of phase the Weirdboy has +2 Strength and +2 Attacks.. Frazzle: Psychic weapon, Shooting, Template, S5, AP4, Assault 1, Pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Weirdboy Discipline" id="517b-da3c-94f0-96a2" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>In addition to the Power of da Waaagh! powers above, a Weirdboy generates psychic abilities randomly. Before deployment, roll one D3 on the Weirdboy Psychic Powers table and one D3 on the Weirdboy Psychic Weapons table. The Weirdboy gains the generated power and weapon for the duration of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Focus" id="878b-3930-69ea-803b" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Before making any To Hit rolls with a Psychic Weapon, the Weirdboy must make a Psychic check. If the check is passed, the Weirdboy may attack normally with the selected weapon. If the check is failed: the Weirdboy suffers Perils of the Warp and may not use the Psychic Weapon during that phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shock Pulse" id="4ebd-ffa3-4b97-f525" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>Any unit that suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from this weapon suffers −1 WS until the end of the next Assault phase. Power: Kind, Phase, Effect. Da Jump: Psychic power, Movement, D3 roll of 1. Instead of moving during the Movement phase, select one friendly Ork Infantry unit within 12". Remove that unit from the battlefield and immediately redeploy it using the Deep Strike special rules. The redeployed unit gains Fleet (2) until the end of the turn. If the Psychic check is failed, the unit scatters D6" and suffers D6 Strength 4 AP – hits.. Waaagh! Pulse: Psychic power, Shooting, D3 roll of 2. Instead of making a Shooting Attack, all friendly Ork units within 12" gain Furious Charge (2) and Dakka! (5+) until the beginning of the controlling player's next turn. If the Psychic check is failed, all affected units become Pinned.. Green Fury: Psychic power, Shooting, D3 roll of 3. Instead of making a Shooting Attack, select one friendly Ork Infantry unit within 12". That unit gains Counter-Attack (1), Crusader and Fearless until the beginning of the controlling player's next turn. If the Psychic check is failed, the affected unit suffers −1 Weapon Skill until the beginning of the controlling player's next turn.. Roll a D3: 1 Green Lightning, 2 Warphead Blast, 3 Fists of Gork. Weapon: Range, Str, AP, Type. Green Lightning: 18", 7, 4, Assault D3, Shock Pulse, Psychic Focus. Warphead Blast: 24", 8, 3, Heavy 1, Large Blast (5"), Gets Hot, Psychic Focus. Fists of Gork: –, x2, 2, Melee, Brutal (2), Psychic Focus.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mishap" id="d1d2-4a94-ee76-f561" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When firing a Shokk Attack Gun, roll 2D6 to determine the weapon's Strength characteristic and a D6 to determine its AP. If the result contains any Double, resolve the attack normally and then immediately roll a D6 on the following Mishap Table. D6: Mishap Result, Rules Effect. 1: Warp Core Collapse!, The firer and every model in the entire unit suffer a Strength 6 AP4 hit with the Deflagrate special rule. The Shokk Attack Gun may not be fired again for the remainder of the battle.. 2: Polarity Reversed, Remove the firer from play and immediately place him in base contact with the target enemy unit. The firer counts as having successfully Charged and becomes Locked in combat, but begins the combat Pinned.. 3: Snotling Rain, The original attack causes no damage. Instead place a Massive Blast (7") template centered on the target. Every unit touched by the template must immediately take a Pinning test.. 4: Ear-Biting Madness, If the target is a Vehicle, it immediately suffers a Crew Shaken result. If the target is Infantry, Cavalry or a Dreadnought, the target gains Blind and Concussive (1) until the end of the next player turn.. 5: Subatomic Materialization, The attack resolves at Strength 10 and gains Fleshbane and Sunder. After resolving the attack, the firer suffers one automatic Wound with no saves of any kind allowed.. 6: Annihilation Vortex, The attack resolves at Strength 10 AP1 and gains Instant Death. The target unit must immediately take a Morale check at -2 Leadership..</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Squig Prodder" id="c04a-b927-5f75-4630" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>A Squig Prodder is a vicious shock stave used to drive attack squigs and terrified Gretchin into uncontrollable aggression. Friendly Gretchin units within 6" of one or more models equipped with a squig prodder gain Furious Charge (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Killsaw" id="d7fe-7293-311a-6d97" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>A model equipped with two Killsaws gains +2 Attacks instead of the normal +1 Attack granted for being armed with two close combat weapons. Grots never gain +1 Attack for being armed with two melee weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Klan (X)" id="a734-620c-db79-3594" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>When building an army, choose one Klan for its Primary Detachment; an Allied Detachment may choose a different Klan. Every unit in that detachment with the Mob Rule special rule, and every Ork vehicle and Dreadnought, gains Klan (X), where X is the chosen Klan. Gretchin units and Gretchin crew never gain Klan (X).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="85f3-c187-c717-378e" hidden="false" publicationId="96d0-c462-d158-fbad">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
